"""
Torre Emperador Castellana (ex Torre Espacio; Q1364354), Cuatro Torres Business Area, Madrid — built by code.

Author: Álvaro C. Chulvi (with AI assistance). Licence of the resulting model: CC BY 4.0.
The building: Pei Cobb Freed & Partners, design partner Henry N. Cobb (1926–2020), 2004–2008 — protected.

Measurements (see meta.json for the sources):
- OpenStreetMap way 98280735 (outline, 42.7 × 42.3 m) and its building:part ways, one per floor: ground floor
  0–4 m, floors 1–3 to 16 m, 4–5 to 24 m, then every floor 4 m high up to floor 50 (204 m) and the top part,
  floors 51–57, to 230 m (Wikipedia: 230 m, 57 floors). Read together, the floors show the rule of the plan:
  a square at the foot whose two opposite corners are cut away, floor by floor, by flat faces that slide across
  the plan until only the lens between two quarter-circle façades is left at the top («a square that turns into
  the intersection of two curves», es.wikipedia); the two other corners stay sharp all the way up.
  The tower is built as one smooth loft through those floor plans: the square, the lens (the plan of floors
  51–57) and, for every floor, where the two cut faces stand (taken from its OSM outline), joined linearly
  between floors.
- The porch: floors 1–3 are cut back to the lens on the south-east corner, a 16 m high porch held by
  a corner pier (way 307857391), with two low glass boxes of the ground floor in it.
- Dark grey-blue glass curtain wall with vertical mullions (every 2.4 m on fixed vertical lines, so they stay
  vertical where the plan changes) and a lighter floor line at every slab.
Simplified: the small notches at the two sharp corners are left out; the roof is flat with a metal coping (no
roof equipment); the porch boxes are the ground floor outline as mapped.

Heading: the porch where the ground floor is set back for the entrance opens to the east and south-east, towards
the ring road of the Cuatro Torres, so the main façade (+Z) is the east face: heading 101.5° (OSM long axis
101.5°). The Paseo de la Castellana is behind it (west).

Axes (docs/MODEL_SPEC.md): +Y up, the east face looks +Z, +X points north-north-east (11.5°);
origin = centroid of the OSM outline.

    python model_sources/Q1364354_torre_emperador_castellana.py   -> models/Q1364354/model.glb
"""
